  {
   "key": "state",
   "title": "State verbs · no -ing",
   "tags": {
    "content": [
     "Present Continuous",
     "Present Simple"
    ],
    "levels": [
     "A1"
    ],
    "skills": [
     "Leitura"
    ]
   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "ATTENTION · VERBS WITHOUT -ING",
    "html": "Some verbs talk about <b>feelings, opinions and what you have</b>. We usually <b>don't</b> use them with -ing, even when it is right now:<br><br><span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>like</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>love</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>hate</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>want</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>need</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>know</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>understand</b></span> · <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>have</b></span> (= ter)<br><br>✗ I am liking this class. → ✓ I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>like</b></span> this class.<br>✗ She is wanting a coffee. → ✓ She <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>wants</b></span> a coffee.<br>✗ I am understanding. → ✓ I <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>understand</b></span>.<br><br>But: I <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>have</b></span> a car (= ter) × I am <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>having</b></span> lunch (= comer). With food and drinks, have + -ing is OK!"
   }
  },
